\ Exercise the AOT native fallback paths reached through compiled words.
\ Two emission sites are covered:
\
\   1. `emitNativeWordCall` (category `native`) when the inline fast
\      path can prove only one operand type and the comparison resolves
\      via the polymorphic native (e.g. string / type-value / boolean
\      operands of `=` or `<`).
\   2. `emitPerOperationFallback` (category `per-op-native`) when both
\      operands look numeric but the three-way arithmetic path falls
\      through to the polymorphic native (mixed fixnum/float `+`).
\
\ In AOT mode both sites now route through `jitNativeWordCall`, so the
\ `--compilation-stats` static-check should report
\ `jitInterpretedCall=0/0` with a non-zero `jitNativeWordCall` count.
\
\ Results are dropped to keep the program free of stream-write / print
\ compound chains; runtime correctness is asserted by exit code rather
\ than printed output.

add:    ( a b -- c ) [ + ] ;
cmp-eq: ( a b -- ? ) [ = ] ;
cmp-lt: ( a b -- ? ) [ < ] ;

\ Mixed fixnum/float arithmetic: drives `emitPerOperationFallback`.
3 2.5 add drop
2.5 3 add drop

\ String comparisons: drive `emitResolvedNativeCallback` in the
\ compiled body of `cmp-eq` / `cmp-lt`.
"abc" "abc" cmp-eq drop
"abc" "xyz" cmp-eq drop
"abc" "xyz" cmp-lt drop

\ Type-value comparisons take the same resolved-native path.
fixnum fixnum cmp-eq drop
fixnum float cmp-eq drop

\ Boolean comparisons.
t t cmp-eq drop
t f cmp-eq drop
